Thanks Mathieu. The rule is right and I kept it as is; I reworded its message while rebasing (d293326b201), because the stated rationale overstated the case: for an ID token read from the direct TLS-validated response of the token endpoint, OIDC Core 1.0 Section 3.1.3.7 (item 6) allows skipping the signature check for any client type, so "no guarantee that the provider issued it" was not accurate. What justifies the rule is defense in depth: a public client is the setup with the fewest safeguards left, and `required: false` buys nothing since the JWKS is cached. The message now says that and names the remedy, and the `required` option's info text mentions the rule so `config:dump-reference` tells the whole story.

Note for merging: #65814 adds its own public-client rule in the same `validate()` chain; I ran the combined merge locally with both suites green, the conflict resolves by keeping both blocks.
